`camera_event_report/models/ssd_mobilenet_v1_12.onnx`

| | |
|---|---|
| Upstream | [ONNX Model Zoo](https://github.com/onnx/models) — `validated/vision/object_detection_segmentation/ssd-mobilenetv1` |
| Source URL | https://github.com/onnx/models/raw/main/validated/vision/object_detection_segmentation/ssd-mobilenetv1/model/ssd_mobilenet_v1_12.onnx |
| SHA256 | `b8fba5e404077d4048d27fcd1667e85e27e192eb9bf51e696c46a3acd7d21058` |
| Size | 28.1 MB |
| Training data | MS COCO 2017 |
| Licence | **MIT** (per the model card; the ONNX Model Zoo repository is Apache-2.0) |

The model's licence is compatible with this repository's MIT licence, so the
weights may be redistributed with the add-on.

### Interface

Taken from the graph itself rather than documentation, since the exported names
differ from the model card:

- Input: one `uint8` tensor, NHWC `(1, height, width, 3)`, dynamic height and
  width. Raw pixels — the graph does its own resize and normalisation.
- Outputs, which must be requested **by name** (positional order is not
  boxes/classes/scores/num): `detection_boxes`, `detection_classes`,
  `detection_scores`, `num_detections`.
- Class ids follow the TensorFlow Object Detection API convention and are
  **1-based**: person is class `1`.

A quantised `ssd_mobilenet_v1_12-int8.onnx` (9.2 MB) exists upstream. It scores
marginally higher on well-lit frames but degrades further on dark, low-contrast
ones — the conditions this add-on most often works in — so the fp32 model is
bundled instead.

